  "term": "ninth cranial nerve",
  "definition": "The ninth cranial nerve is the glossopharyngeal nerve, a nerve with both sensory and motor functions. It carries signals involved in swallowing, salivary gland activity, taste and sensation from the back third of the tongue and nearby throat areas, and sensory input from the carotid sinus.",
